  "claim_boundary": "Fresh paired MuJoCo S3 pilot only. This pilot has no fine-tuned full-loop gate pass: direction-head calibration improvements did not recover either size's registered full-loop gate. Under this contract, a future fine-tuned pass could show sufficiency for that simulated gate; necessity would additionally require both zero-shot and calibration-only to fail the same frozen gate. This cannot establish that real-robot data fine-tuning is necessary: no real F/T sample, manufacturing tolerance, passivity, motor coupling, threading, or extraction is represented. The privileged straight-to-center arm is an execution gate, not a guaranteed performance upper bound: its direct path can itself hard-stop. Strict success also includes offline true-center/contact-tag capture validation; that scorer is not available to non-oracle controllers and is not a deployable terminal signal. Hyperparameter/model selection was not independently preregistered, so a future positive necessity claim would require a frozen or nested model-selection protocol.",
